### What was modified

The set is **not** vendored verbatim, and the MIT licence permits the changes. Monge draws each
piece three times over — a `boundary` path, a `main` path with identical geometry, and a blurred
drop shadow — plus decorative line work, and the upstream source ships `#ff0000` and `#00ff00` as
stroke and fill placeholders because the set is built to be recoloured. So:

- `boundary` is dropped. It is the same geometry as `main` under a heavier stroke, and the board
  already draws an outline of its own.
- The drop shadow is dropped. It is a Gaussian blur filter, and requirement F5 mounts one preview
  board per reply — thirty-two blurred pieces per board, twenty boards on a branch point.
- Every colour is removed, so fill and stroke come from the design tokens and a piece's colour is
  not part of its shape.
- Each role's decorative paths are concatenated into one. A path that opens with a relative moveto
  is prefixed with `M0 0` so that concatenation does not move it; uppercasing the `m` instead would
  turn its implicit trailing linetos absolute and draw a scribble.

The shapes are on Monge's 933-unit grid, not the conventional 45-unit one. Colour is not part of a
shape: `<use>` supplies the fill and stroke, so each of the six shapes serves both its white and
its black piece, and the two invert against each other in greyscale.

### Which sets were considered, and why not those

Every licence below was read from lichess's `COPYING.md` rather than from a summary, and the
candidates were rendered on a real board at both sizes this application uses — the main board and
the 96px branch preview, where a preview square is twelve pixels and detail collapses.

| Set          | Licence           | Verdict                                                                                                                             |
| ------------ | ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **celtic**   | **MIT**           | **Chosen.** A conventional Staunton silhouette despite the name; one geometry per role for both colours; 3.6KB of path data in total |
| `chessnut`   | Apache 2.0        | Usable, and the cleanest at full size. Its king and queen are both crowns, and at twelve pixels its bishop and king are one blob     |
| `rhosgfx`    | CC0 1.0           | Usable, and asks nothing at all. A chunky game-asset style rather than a chess set; its king reads as a bottle                       |
| `spatial`    | MIT, same author  | Usable. Hand-sketched; the queen reads as a tuft of grass and the white king nearly vanishes at preview size                         |
| `fantasy`    | MIT, same author  | Usable. Illustrative, 71KB of source, and king and queen are again both crowns                                                       |
| `kiwen-suwi` | CC BY 4.0         | Usable but attribution-bearing, and it is flat fills with no outline — the one thing the greyscale requirement cannot do without     |
| `cburnett`   | **GPLv2+**        | Rejected. The lichess default, and the same copyleft risk ADR-0003 rejected chessground and chessops over                            |
| `merida`     | **GPLv2+**        | Rejected, same reason                                                                                                               |
| `letter`, `pirouetti`, `pixel` | **AGPLv3+** | Rejected, same reason and stronger                                                                                |
| `mpchess`    | **GPLv3+**        | Rejected, same reason                                                                                                               |
| `shapes`     | CC BY-SA 4.0      | Rejected. Share-alike on the artwork                                                                                                |
| `maestro`, `caliente`, `fresca`, `gioco`, `staunty`, `dubrovny`, `cardinal`, `anarcandy`, `icpieces`, `california`, `cooke`, `horsey`, `tatiana`, `monarchy`, `minimal-warmth`, `disguised`, `xkcd` | **CC BY-NC-SA** | Rejected. Non-commercial, which this project does not accept |
