## Stockfish

`public/engine/` — `stockfish-19-lite-single.js`, `stockfish-19-lite-single.wasm`

**Origin:** the release files of [stockfish.js](https://github.com/nmrugg/stockfish.js) 19.0.0
by Nathan Rugg and Chess.com (npm `stockfish@19.0.0`, commit
`54fde71d90c7c403964f6cacef48f7bbec495df1`), a WebAssembly build of
[Stockfish](https://github.com/official-stockfish/Stockfish) by the Stockfish developers, with the
`nn-61e7af4bb97d` network by Chris Bao embedded. Vendored unmodified.
**Licence:** GNU General Public License, version 3 (`public/engine/COPYING.txt`).
**Why GPL code sits in an MIT repository, and why that does not make the application GPL:**
ADR-0012. In short: Stockfish is a separate program. The analysis page starts it as a Web Worker
from its own URL and exchanges UCI text with it; nothing in `src/` imports, bundles or links its
code. That reading of the GPL is common among chess sites and is not legal advice.
**What the licence obliges us to do, and where it is done:** convey the licence with the program,
and make the corresponding source available. `COPYING.txt` and `public/engine/README.md` are
published beside the engine on the deployed site, and the README names the exact upstream
release, commit and network, with each file's SHA-256. `tools/engine/vendored.test.ts` holds the
files to those hashes, so the engine cannot change without this notice being wrong in a way CI
reports. The About page credits it and links to both.
